# ============================================================
# Test: FireDustInteraction1
# Description: Fire and dust with active fire-dust coupling
#              (fire_dust_coupling = true) using lagged wind coupling.
#              Fire burned areas reduce the dust crust index,
#              leading to modified dust emission in post-fire zones.
#              Flat terrain, no terrain wind.
#
# Grid ratios: dust.grid_ratio = fire.grid_ratio = 2
#   (16x16 dust/fire grid over 3000 m domain, dx=187.5 m)
#   REQUIRED: dust.grid_ratio must equal fire.grid_ratio when
#   fire_dust_coupling=true, otherwise burned cells are sub-grid
#   on the dust grid and crust reduction has no effect. An assertion
#   in the code enforces this and aborts if they differ.
#
# Ignition: ignition_r = 600 m marks ~32 burned fire cells at t=0
#   (~12.5% of the 256-cell fire domain).
#
# Crust reduction: fire_dust_crust_reduction = 0.99
#   Burned cells: crust drops from 1.0 -> 0.01 (nearly bare soil).
#   Unburned cells: crust = 1.0 (fully protected).
#
# Expected Results (verified step=20, t=10 s, dt=0.5 s, 4096 atm cells):
#
#   Dynamics:
#   - Simulation completes 20 steps without errors.
#   - Fixed dt = 0.5 s.
#   - u*_max ~ 1.121 m/s  |  u_10m_max ~ 14.99 m/s
#   - PBLH_max ~ 535.4 m  |  T_sfc ~ 300 K (slight warming from fire)
#
#   Fire (step 20):
#   - Fire ignites at (1500, 1500) with radius 600 m and spreads outward.
#   - Number of active fire cells: 32
#   - Lagged coupling: fire spread uses wind from previous atm timestep.
#   - Fire heat flux injected: Q_atm_max = 3522 W/m^2 (alfg=45 m)
#   - RhoTheta tendency sum ~ 2.027 kg K m^-3 s^-1
#   - EddyDiff::Scalar_v_max = 13.618 m^2/s  (vs 2.168 in baseline: +528%)
#   - Surface temp max: 300.60 K (heated by fire)
#
#   Dust Threshold (step 20):
#   - Per-cell u*_t varies with crust:
#     u*_t_min = 0.004741 m/s  (burned cells, crust=0.01)
#     u*_t_max = 0.007111 m/s  (unburned cells, crust=1.0)
#   - This confirms per-cell crust modulation is working correctly.
#
#   Dust Emission (step 20):
#   - emission_sum = 1.190330e-05 kg/s
#   - Compared to FireDustBaseline (1.234186e-05 kg/s): -3.5%
#   - The coupled emission is LOWER because the fire heat flux raises
#     EddyDiff 6x (13.6 vs 2.2 m^2/s), increasing PBL mixing and
#     dispersing near-surface dust faster. The crust reduction in 32
#     burned cells lowers u*_t locally but the dominant effect at t=10 s
#     is the fire-driven BL deepening reducing near-surface concentration.
#   - emission_flux bin0 max = 4.651e-08 kg/m^2/s
#   - F_dust_atm_max = 1.396e-07 kg/m^2/s (vs 1.447e-07 in baseline)
#
#   Dust Concentrations (step 20):
#   - conc_sfc_max ~ 81.9 ug/m^3  (vs ~84.7 in baseline: -3.3%)
#   - PM10_max ~ 77.7 ug/m^3
#   - RHO DUST = 11.944  (vs 12.379 in baseline: -3.5%)
#   - All dust concentrations non-negative.
#
#   Mass Budget (step 20):
#   - MASS = 1.013e+10  |  RHO THETA = 3.080496e+12  (higher than baseline)
#   - RHO SCALAR = 0
#
#   Performance:
#   - Timestep wall time ~ 6.2e-03 s  |  Total ~ 0.147 s
# ============================================================

erf.prob_name = "ABL"
